.TH MODBUS-SCRAPER 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-scraper \- Prometheus exporter for Huawei SUN2000 inverters
(Modbus TCP, stdlib only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-scraper
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Prometheus exporter for Huawei SUN2000 inverters (Modbus TCP, stdlib
only). Polls the inverter over Modbus TCP and serves the huawei_* metrics
the dashboard expects at /metrics in the Prometheus text format: the PV
generation, the grid exchange (import/export split), the home consumption
implied by the balance, the battery (optional) and the health gauges
(scraper_up, the error counter, the last poll age).
.PP
Every poll is sanity-checked: a negative PV reading, an array larger than
\fB--max-kwp\fR, a grid line beyond \fB--max-grid-kw\fR or a negative
home balance marks the exposition \fB503\fR (the sensors are suspect, not
the poller) and names the register in the log. A modbus-cache in front of
the device is detected automatically (its synthesized diagnostics block)
and adds the device-up / cache-age / cache-uptime gauges.
.PP
Modbus auth (\fB--auth\fR): with \fBsuite\fR the session proves the
shared key (\fB--auth-key\fR, min 16 characters) with a crypt handshake
right after every connect \(em 52 bytes: magic, fresh nonce,
HMAC\-SHA256 proof; the peer answers \fBOK\fR and plain Modbus follows,
or \fBERR\fR and the connection fails (the poller keeps retrying).
Empty auth (the default) = no auth at all.
.PP
The exposition endpoint is the tool's serving surface: the connection caps
(\fB--max-clients\fR total, \fB--max-conn-per-ip\fR per peer, extras
get an immediate 503), the idle keep-alive kick (\fB--client-timeout\fR)
and the bearer token (\fB--auth-token\fR, the value a token or a
\fBfile:<path>\fR reference). A
non-loopback listen without a token refuses to start (F13 in
docs/AUDIT.md).
.PP
The JSON-lines control server (\fB--control-port\fR, talked to with
\fBmodbus-scraper-ctl\fR(1) and \fBmodbus-scraper-cli\fR(1)) inspects
and steers the running exporter: the live settings, an immediate poll, the
config reload, the Modbus session restart, the graceful shutdown. With a
control token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: every command and reply
carries the full sha256 of its payload, keyed by the token
(common/wiresec.py) \(em a token-holding client verifies both directions,
and over TCP the signed commands are mandatory. A second, read-only token
(\fB--control-ops-token\fR) authenticates into the show/clear verbs only
\(em the ops shift against the admin key, both roles audited.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-upstream
the inverter Modbus TCP endpoint HOST:PORT (`:5502` = 127.0.0.1:5502)
(default: config, $UPSTREAM or 127.0.0.1:5502)
.TP
.BI \-\-modbus\-unit " N"
Modbus unit id (default: config, $MODBUS_UNIT or 1)
.TP
.BI \-\-modbus\-offset " N"
added to register addresses (default: config, $MODBUS_OFFSET or 0)
.TP
.B \-\-auth
the inverter's Modbus auth scheme: `suite` proves the shared auth\-key
with a crypt handshake right after every connect (the peer answers OK,
or ERR and the connection fails — the poller keeps retrying); none/empty
= no auth at all (default: config, $AUTH or none)
.TP
.B \-\-auth\-key
the shared key the suite handshake proves (min 16 characters); the value
may be `file:<path>` — the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file (a
systemd LoadCredential rides as file:/run/credentials/...) (default:
config, $AUTH_KEY)
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
Modbus timeout in seconds (default: config, $TIMEOUT or 3)
.TP
.B \-\-profile
device profile JSON (the shared profiles/ schema; scrape\-marked entries
feed the metric registers) (default: config, $PROFILE or the bundled
sun2000 profile)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-spec
metrics spec JSON, sectioned: {profile: {key: {help, profile?}},
compute: ..., scraper: ...} — merged in memory over the built\-in
lib/metrics.json scraper_* block (default: config, $METRICS_SPEC or the
bundled metrics.json)
.TP
.B \-\-metric\-prefix
the prefix on the profile\- and compute\-fed metric names (default:
config, $METRIC_PREFIX or 'huawei'); the bundled scraper_* names are
fixed
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-kwp " N"
maximum PV array kWp (default: config, $MAX_KWP or 6; 0 = no checking)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-grid\-kw " N"
maximum grid kW, either direction (default: config, $MAX_GRID_KW or 12;
0 = no checking)
.TP
.B \-\-battery
enable battery support (default: config, $BATTERY or off)
.TP
.B \-\-grid\-positive\-import
grid register positive when importing (default: config,
$GRID_POSITIVE_IMPORT or positive = export)
.TP
.B \-\-listen
listen address HOST:PORT (default: config, $LISTEN or 127.0.0.1:9350)
.TP
.B \-\-local\-time
log timestamps in the system time zone instead of UTC (default: off)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-clients " N"
maximum concurrent HTTP clients; extras get an immediate 503 (default:
config, $MAX_CLIENTS or 64; 0 = unlimited)
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-timeout " N"
seconds an idle keep\-alive HTTP client is kept before being kicked
(default: config, $CLIENT_TIMEOUT or 300; 0 = off)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-conn\-per\-ip " N"
maximum concurrent HTTP connections from one peer IP; extras get an
immediate 503 (default: config, $MAX_CONN_PER_IP or 0 = no per\-IP
limit)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
JSON\-lines control server target: unix socket path (default:
/tmp/modbus\-scraper\-<listen\-port>.socket) or TCP port number on
127.0.0.1 (e.g. 15599); 0 = off. Talk to it with modbus\-scraper\-ctl.py
(default: config, $CTL)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
require a token on control connections: the client authenticates with
{"cmd": "auth", "token": ...}; over the unix socket a trusted peer
(root, the daemon's own user or \-\-control\-trust\-uids — SO_PEERCRED)
skips the token; the value may be `file:<path>` — the first line of an
owner\-only 0600 file (a systemd LoadCredential rides as
file:/run/credentials/...) (default: config, $CONTROL_TOKEN or none)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-ops\-token
a second, read\-only control token: sessions authenticating with it may
run the show/clear verbs only (no set/unset, no poll now, no request
reload, no restart, no shutdown) — the ops shift against the admin key,
both audited; the value may be `file:<path>` — the first line of an
owner\-only 0600 file (a systemd LoadCredential rides as
file:/run/credentials/...) (default: config, $CONTROL_OPS_TOKEN or none)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-ops\-verbs
the read\-only ops role's RBAC policy: the verbs its sessions may run,
comma\-separated (default: show,clear; validated against the control
grammar at start)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-trust\-uids
extra peer uids the unix control socket trusts without the token
(SO_PEERCRED — a local systemd unit speaks without the secret); root and
the daemon's own user are always trusted (default: config,
$CONTROL_TRUST_UIDS or none)
.TP
.B \-\-auth\-token
require Authorization: Bearer <token> on all requests; the value may be
`file:<path>` — the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file (a systemd
LoadCredential rides as file:/run/credentials/...) (default: config,
$AUTH_TOKEN or disabled)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
SCR audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout (the docker/journald way);
default: the XDG state home (~/.local/state/modbus\-scraper/audit.log)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size in MB, keeping 3 backups; 0 = no size
rotation (default 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the SCR audit trail (default: off)
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " N"
seconds between polls (default: config, $INTERVAL or 10)
.TP
.B \-\-log\-access
log every HTTP request at INFO (default: config, $LOG_ACCESS or quiet)
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level
log level (default: config, $LOG_LEVEL or INFO)
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-path
the state dump: the live setting overrides (the poll plan, the caps, the
log surface — the tokens apart) as one JSON, written 0600 with an
integrity hash (a restore refuses a tampered, unsigned or
group\-writable dump); dumped on the request dump command and the
graceful shutdown; loaded on start only with \-\-restore\-on\-start, on
demand with the request restore command (default: config, $DUMP_PATH or
none)
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-key
the key that seals the state dumps and the reload's state file: the
state rides encrypted (an HMAC\-SHA256 counter\-mode keystream,
authenticated — a restore refuses a wrong or missing key, and a
configured key refuses an unsealed dump); the reload re\-exec
re\-resolves the same key, so the state file reads on the other side; no
key = the dumps stay 0600 plaintext with the integrity hash a dump path
without a key warns at start and on set; the value may be `file:<path>`
— the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file (a systemd LoadCredential
rides as file:/run/credentials/...) (default: config, $DUMP_KEY or none)
.TP
.B \-\-restore\-on\-start
load the state dump when the daemon starts (needs \-\-dump\-path) — the
live overrides ride again instead of a cold start; default: start cold,
load only on demand (default: config, $RESTORE_ON_START) (default: off)
.TP
.B \-\-config
config file — the set grammar: every line a `set <name> <value>`,
comments start with # (default: $CONFIG, then scraper.conf next to this
script, then the subproject root) (default:
/Users/oom/GensparkCode/pv\-dash/scraper/scraper.conf)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
validate the configuration, print the effective settings and exit
(nothing is bound or connected) (default: off)


.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
re-read the config file (and the auth token file) and apply what is live
(the same path as the control server's request reload); a broken config
keeps the previous settings.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
graceful shutdown.

.SH CONTROL
The control server speaks JSON lines ({"cmd": "..."} ->
{"status": "ok|err|bye", "text": "..."}; TCP requires the token when
configured and refuses to start without one). Commands:
\fBset\fR/\fBunset\fR/\fBshow\fR/\fBhelp\fR (the settings: interval,
timeout, max-clients, client-timeout, max-conn-per-ip, log-access,
log-level \(em and the token lives: control token, the ops token,
auth token, each rotating live, the value never rendering \(em
\fBshow <secret>\fR refuses), \fBshow status\fR, \fBshow connections\fR
(the live HTTP clients), \fBshow version\fR, \fBshow knobs\fR
(the dictionary of the registry), \fBpoll now\fR,
\fBinspect\fR, \fBrequest reload\fR (the SIGHUP path),
\fBreload\fR (the whole-daemon restart that keeps the sets: the live
overrides save to a state file beside the config, the process re-execs,
the fresh daemon re-applies them once), with a dump path configured
(\fB--dump-path\fR): \fBrequest dump\fR / \fBrequest restore\fR
(the overrides as one 0600 integrity-hashed JSON; \fB--dump-key\fR
seals it \(em the state rides encrypted, a restore refuses a wrong or
missing key; \fB--restore-on-start\fR
loads it at start), \fBrestart\fR, \fBshutdown\fR,
\fBquit\fR. See
.BR modbus-scraper-ctl (1)
and
.BR modbus-scraper-cli (1).

.SH SECURITY
The scraper reads an open Modbus device (no auth, no TLS — the inverter's
network isolation is the boundary) and serves /metrics: bind loopback by
default, set the bearer token when it must serve beyond loopback (a
non-loopback token-less start is refused, F13), and keep the connection
caps on. The control surface is loopback-only (TCP) or a 0600 unix socket;
a TCP control port without a token refuses to start (F5); with a token the
wire is signed and the commands/replies verify end to end; a second,
read-only ops token (\fB--control-ops-token\fR) scopes its sessions to
the show/clear verbs. The audit trail (default in the XDG state home,
prefix SCR) records the control commands with their roles, the auth
failures, the reloads and the shutdowns.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/modbus-scraper-<listen-port>.socket
the default control socket.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/modbus-scraper/audit.log
the default audit trail.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-scraper-ctl (1),
.BR modbus-scraper-cli (1),
.BR modbus-cache (1),
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1)
.PP
scraper/README.md in the suite checkout \(em the full documentation.
